// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Two-phase span-aware strategy with budget-guarded forced closure.
//
// Observations from prior failures:
//   - 7 examples generated hundreds of `!` tokens inside constrained spans,
//     exhausting the step budget before `>>` was emitted.
//   - 5 examples opened `<<` but never emitted `>>` before the budget ran out.
//   - 28 examples produced syntactically valid but semantically wrong expressions.
//
// Design:
//   Outside spans: free UnconstrainedStep until `<<` is detected by RenderedEndsWith.
//   Inside spans (budget > closeReserve): SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep with penalty 4.0
//     to break the `!`-repetition dead-end loop observed in prior failures.
//     Close immediately when parser.IsCompletePrefix is satisfied.
//   Budget guard: when remaining steps <= closeReserve AND inside a span, delegate
//     to CloseSpanWithinBudget which is dead-end-aware, tracks the longest completable
//     prefix, and emits `>>` before the budget expires.
//   Final cleanup: after loop exit, if still inside a span with budget remaining,
//     call CloseSpanWithinBudget again.
//   Prompt guidance: emphasize int(), exact variable names, and no premature simplification.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 – parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   (remaining <= closeReserve branch): CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition guarantees
//     `insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut)`. Preserved on both closed and
//     still-open exit paths. ✓
//
//   (outside span branch): If next != eosToken and RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<"),
//     we set currentConstrainedOut := [], which satisfies IsValidPrefix([]) by the
//     method precondition. Otherwise insideConstrainedOut stays false (vacuous). ✓
//
//   (complete prefix branch): CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false,
//     making the implication vacuously true. ✓
//
//   (constrained step branch): SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep returns either eosToken
//     (we break without state change) or a parser-valid token (by hard-mask postcondition).
//     AppendConstrainedToken's postcondition asserts parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut). ✓
//
//   (final cleanup): Same argument as the closeReserve branch. ✓
//
// Invariant 2 – progress:
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   (remaining <= closeReserve, s = steps_before):
//     CloseSpanWithinBudget(remaining) postcondition: |cg| <= |generated| + remaining.
//     |cg| <= |generatedPrefix| + s + (maxSteps - s) = |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//     After steps := maxSteps: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//
//   (outside): steps grows by 1; at most one token appended to generated. ✓
//   (complete): steps grows by 1; CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one `>>`. ✓
//   (constrained step): steps grows by 1; at most one token appended via AppendConstrainedToken
//     when next != eosToken; break (no append) when next == eosToken. ✓
//   (final cleanup): Same argument as closeReserve branch. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
